# S3 (tonight, plan.md unserve step U3): hand the four cards back to development. DELETE the placement through the
# admin API FIRST and see placements: [] (a warm placement is redispatched by the reconciler); only then push this job.
# platform: captures the serving container's state, env and /v1/models (read-only) into the results.
# unserve:  stops (graceful, 60 s) and removes every thatch-inference-* container (an exited one blocks every CI card
#           step).
# reset:    all four boards together, plus the heal (late switch cards, the telemetry by-id race, a link that did not
#           train). It refuses while any card is held or any thatch-inference-* container exists (unserve, just
#           before it, removes them), so it cannot pull cards out from under a live or starting container.
# Nothing else is changed: the drop-in stays P150x4 and zot's thatch-serving-tt:latest stays the TP4 layer. After this
# reset the QSFP gate is stale again, which is the overnight safety net: no container can start on the cards even if a
# placement reappeared. Tonight's fabric check is tt-measure-links.yml with apply=false (plan.md U4).
# Tomorrow's re-serve is S4 + re-measure (apply=true) + /deploy, with no rebuild if the image is unchanged.
# C1 as in S1. Duration: status 1-2 min, platform 1 min, unserve 1-2 min, reset 3-12 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status platform unserve reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-g1-C1
C2_PROFILE=general-prefix-tp4
